# Optional overrides for `npm run dev` (copy to react/.env.local, which is gitignored).
# Local development needs no Amplify sandbox and no amplify_outputs.json. Full steps:
# README.md, "Local development". Nothing in this file is a secret.

# --- Backend ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `vite dev` uses Django by default; it is the only backend (the Amplify Data build was removed).
# VITE_BACKEND=django

# --- Django port --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Vite proxy sends /api to http://127.0.0.1:$DJANGO_DEV_PORT (default 8010). Prefer setting
# DJANGO_DEV_PORT once in the repository-root .env: `make runserver` binds the same value, so the
# two cannot disagree. Set it here only to override that for Vite.
# DJANGO_DEV_PORT=8000
# Or a full loopback origin, which wins over DJANGO_DEV_PORT:
# DJANGO_DEV_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# --- Cognito (parent sign-in) -------------------------------------------------------------------
# The existing user pool and its public web app client (no secret). If these are unset, `vite dev`
# uses COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID and the first COGNITO_ALLOWED_CLIENT_IDS entry from the root .env,
# which Django already needs, so you normally write them only once there.
# VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=us-west-2_XXXXXXXXX
# VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# --- Vite port ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_DEV_PORT=5183
